ion=extraction_instruction, context=self.problem_text)\n\n        # Step 2: Calculate commission for each newspaper type\n        commission_instruction = f"""\n        Given the extracted information: {extracted_info}\n        Calculate the commission earned for each type of newspaper separately. \n        For the New York Times, multiply the number of copies by the commission rate and the price per copy. \n        Repeat the same process for the Wall Street Journal. \n        Ensure that the calculations are accurate and include all necessary steps.\n        """\n        commission_results = await asyncio.gather(\n            self.generate(instruction=commission_instruction, context=self.problem_text),\n            self.generate(instruction=commission_instruction, context=self.problem_text)\n        )\n\n        # Step 3: Summarize the commission results\n        summarize_instruction = """\n        Summarize the commission results for both newspapers. \n        Ensure that the summary includes the total commission earned from each newspaper and the combined total.\n        Present the results clearly and concisely.\n        """\n        summarized_results = await self.summarize(instruction=summarize_instruction, context=commission_results[0])\n\n        # Step 4: Ensemble to select the final answer\n        ensemble_instruction = """\n        Evaluate the summarized results and select the final answer. \n        Ensure that the answer is a single numerical value representing the total commission earned. \n        Verify that the answer makes sense in the context of the problem.\n        """\n        final_answer = await self.ensemble(instruction=ensemble_instruction, contexts=[summarized_results])\n\n        return final_answer\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.p